"c0b79234-b6e9-558f-ad93-cef54a670397" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553598 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125058 :question/id #uuid "6b5330de-42e9-59fc-85b7-be3de824baa9"} :step/id #uuid "0de063b2-395e-543a-987f-5a9f09cd0abc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553647}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553605 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351264 :question/id #uuid "725672f2-a45d-5f52-bf51-6290d583f846"} :step/id #uuid "1d688f90-2156-50fe-abce-767206c2a691"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553647 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323922 :question/id #uuid "2975c4f9-6dee-5125-bb13-6ec3dea74ab8"} :step/id #uuid "8de53475-1851-510f-9270-5e2d806f8abb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553664}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553664 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488273 :question/id #uuid "deae4223-84c9-5248-9dcf-afbc4aa0a08d"} :step/id #uuid "b6db807e-2397-57e2-bc90-d8c26b85b92f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553666}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553666 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323925 :question/id #uuid "2c8cda82-c43a-5e00-b3a6-861564481ae4"} :step/id #uuid "bea2a768-29f7-5eb9-ac35-6df016064c43" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553605}}] :activity/title "Properties of Diagonalization" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552860}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186049678 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124530 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124339 :question/id #uuid "dfb93cc8-6bf0-59d4-8fbc-c94f5c0c1a69" :question/math-academy-id "e-5502" :question/problem "Find $A^{100},$ where \n![](images/81/81d78f5e129614d85d3719539ab9afc1a04307afb3b03eb9d7a55829ee6354c9.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First,  notice that\n\n![](images/43/43438bad181467e28a2e0758f7b7aa070fd5f5de37e1a6e19d4cabb591dc4f7d.svg)\n\nSo, we have been given the following diagonalization of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/93/93e5e9f9947fb4299da165192f103d7be7494ecc752edacf1a4931d4766337ef.svg)\n\nSince $A=PDP^{-1},$ we can compute $A^k$ by using the formula \n\n$$\nA^{k} = PD^{k}P^{-1}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{100} & =P{D}^{100}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{100}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{1}^{100} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {0}^{100}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "634729e9-7633-52d8-99fa-b00fc9cbe96a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67758f6f-0bf0-51fc-87c0-90fd9ee00d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321953} {:answer/id #uuid "967675ed-4e19-57c8-99ea-021237893dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322346} {:answer/id #uuid "adc0e8ef-12e7-5f5e-becc-f92a32cdaebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322510} {:answer/id #uuid "beab62c6-eabf-50ec-9210-1f331a3c0fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}100 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 100\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322632} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc12535-e7f5-5390-8e16-a0d91cccf389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322346} :answer-field/id #uuid "b46b2ed8-bb1b-55ea-a099-3b79ebaba1ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323520}] :question/id #uuid "6af12003-3389-5965-bc72-a49e9c3974b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-37257" :question/problem "Find ${A}^{101},$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have been given the following diagonalization of $A:$\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSince $A=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${A}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{A}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{101} & =P{D}^{101}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{101}(\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{1}^{101} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (-1)^{101}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5f0e3f-05e4-5b32-8e42-33db9fecfeec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392116} {:answer/id #uuid "afc41b45-077b-59fa-a6a2-e28ef564d7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392117} {:answer/id #uuid "e32ce8d9-f253-5c0c-9791-88ffd609ec43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392118} {:answer/id #uuid "d874ecd1-ed8a-514f-b148-263bd1e5349a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}97 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -97\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392119} {:answer/id #uuid "cd20040e-34e4-5440-afc8-b39be1193ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392118} :answer-field/id #uuid "f73eb74f-7d8e-56f2-a6c1-4e42926c09f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392115}] :question/id #uuid "c7259ad7-f6a1-5f38-87c9-86ba246db7b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-37597" :question/problem "Find ${A}^{97},$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have been given the following diagonalization of $A.$\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $A=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${A}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{A}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{97} & =P{D}^{97}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{97}{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)^{97} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{97}\\end{bmatrix}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c36a09-640e-5f2f-bee6-5e3ec7470874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 9 \\\\ -24 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269293} {:answer/id #uuid "3064e2aa-2353-5c23-8c5a-c90a2e00dae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 9 \\\\ -21 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269705} {:answer/id #uuid "47e19908-9201-5477-8a4f-5d2e1bcb5a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :ans