 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $M=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${M}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{M}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{24} & =P{D}^{24}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[12]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[8]{2}\\end{bmatrix}}^{24}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}(\\sqrt[12]{2})^{24} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[8]{2})^{24}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 40 \\\\ 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-16 & 60 \\\\ -8 & 28\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85014fe6-15e2-5564-bffa-ad90af465709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-29 & 48 \\\\ -20 & 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379805} {:answer/id #uuid "4c043ac2-85b1-59df-a20c-59478e1a4e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379806} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a42728-eef7-5a58-9f94-3c8639fc3ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\be