ain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -16 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -16 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d711e45-7ec3-56d2-ab35-037569a4df11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483744} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8a1859-b3ba-56f4-b537-6223471bd407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483825} {:answer/id #uuid "b8679840-e1d7-55b1-9b60-168dd43e13d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483937} {:answer/id #uuid "db442710-d557-5f6a-8536-d434b1d8713a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484004} {:answer/id #uuid "f05253ae-92cc-554f-a9fa-70f4587815bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 6\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484004} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e61c18c-5fab-5f5b-87cc-ad4a3cb34dce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484155}] :question/id #uuid "988956df-fafe-5af5-9e6f-367acfc61887" :question/math-academy-id "q-42570" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{21}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03920cc4-e1f8-50bf-92b8-43b1b2e14c0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550381} {:answer/id #uuid "240d25dd-ce33-51bd-b4d9-30068b1a023f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550455} {:answer/id #uuid "5f583757-004f-544b-ab61-0bdb788421ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -7 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550600} {:answer/id #uuid "75c87c6c-1364-57a5-9015-96559daffe3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550664} {:answer/id #uuid "9c4798fb-d6a8-5a46-9f8e-17d00a574faf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550381} :answer-field/id #uuid "69e4982b-2aae-5d00-991d-b6494c4a55db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551125}] :question/id #uuid "45127938-c6a2-5a13-8b44-5358b2433862" :question/math-academy-id "q-42930" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{33}=-1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53538eaf-3ca1-53e7-9333-cb61969424e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550565} {:answer/id #uuid "55b5cc00-611f-5c77-a3e4-4fa552b677f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550574} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5a6ba5-deda-5536-8c5f-86d60dc12567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550593} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa3b56-bb47-5f40-b3a8-c0a8da00b436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 14\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550608} {:answer/id #uuid "6d228a6a-bde9-526c-92b6-f3b9c6d2dd53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550638} :answer-field/id #uuid "7975514b-1327-5f70-a5a4-a2499ab3c36c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551137}] :question/id #uuid "adab6899-9f13-599d-9b9d-313f4a53055c" :question/math-academy-id "q-91173" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 14 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 14 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119691 :question/id #uuid "ccf558b9-bf00-58c7-b244-2c5797f93d8e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8060" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Find a $3\\times 3$ determinant that has the same value.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of $a_{23}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{23}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fec93138-cf0b-5d3f-8a5c-8882046ae062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394835} {:answer/id #uuid "090d23f3-9df7-5a18-ad1c-3041ca3b0b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 & 10 \\\\ -9 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394836} {:answer/id #uuid "c4475098-4c19-544f-a8c8-75b11b40afce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394837} {:answer/id #uuid "0720eaf4-1dba-52f4-98df-0fc8cc7f0d92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394838} {:answer/id #uuid "c47f2fc0-2674-5e12-89b3-daeb57faaf22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394835} :answer-field/id #uuid "294d6d11-4a04-5aed-b0e6-84671260549e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394834}] :question/id #uuid "2ea53fce-52af-53d1-b17c-6cd66b5ff019" :question/math-academy-id "q-91092" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -7 & 10 \\\\ -9 & -1 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -7 & 10 \\\\ -9 & -1 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-1){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46cd8000-1e23-5199-b2db-301eb99e864d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394862} {:answer/id #uuid "1289a79f-f03a-57c5-80ce-7fd42973e8bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394863} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2989e5-bdd3-537a-85ba-5abd1555a897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394864} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd0f37a-c44f-5c54-9e1a-bd783a206783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394865} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ae3856-08c7-541a-9fe1-12f594788fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394865} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8b159e-b89f-5a64-b5d5-e5aa63c40762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394861}] :question/id #uuid "d2a2b160-a569-5696-8596-179bbcebb9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-91220" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-1){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0685acda-dabb-560b-835d-974f913cb089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5|\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 11\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263058} {:answer/id #uuid "4abda768-2e36-5ebe-80cd-a6939dc2eb45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 10 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263641} {:answer/id #uuid "722261ce-df60-52c8-870a-f2ed03c31570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263987} {:answer/id #uuid "87f4186d-8c9e-549b-951d-f226a4c88553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264173} {:answer/id #uuid "f93060c2-093d-5765-a883-7a6f9f556b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 13 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263987} :answer-field/id #uuid "743f5871-15a4-5c56-a6e4-6a4075056f59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265445}] :question/id #uuid "a23452bb-a248-5e96-8492-46dd8bc136aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-132024" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 9 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 10 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{14}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{14}=3$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 9 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 10 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-3){C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 11 & -5 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 11 & -5 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "496fac11-29ae-50dd-b6d4-0f5fec7f1e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & -23 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355313} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2f4e07-ac8f-539b-a082-42f26b6fc922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355612} {:answer/id #uuid "7b70ddaf-7367-5f2a-ac12-a6be8b4d9140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355749} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b27742-7bad-5cf1-9d73-f5ea224d0c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356353} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a806ad-64ab-57c6-98f1-817a816d783d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & -23 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355313} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c888b6-8672-574e-a1e9-261cd3ebc924" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357152}] :question/id #uuid "8c88f672-e81c-5620-9a17-5b2addde6eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-91196" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{43}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{43}=-1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-4){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-3){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & 6 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & 7 & -23 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & 6 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & 7 & -23 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+3}|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & -23 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 & -21 \\\\ 17 & -31 & -23 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068749ff-00c0-5411-89ad-26aee923eb5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354711} {:answer/id #uuid "2847d2af-fd66-5233-908b-5eecb31cf46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355002} {:answer/id #uuid "2e98ac02-485c-5d18-b825-9f674d805616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355069} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9ed764-d77f-5c1e-b981-5a63469e8c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355752} {:answer/id #uuid "a0767177-36f3-58b3-bda9-2a7cd1100697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 10 & -10 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 13\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 10 & -10 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 13\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 175921863