e $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254347} {:answer/id #uuid "84ed66fe-a32a-5630-855d-615f22ac4a6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254851} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e3dfd5-c2d6-5991-92f3-12f23124f7af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255995}] :question/id #uuid "8408d555-50d3-5d93-86ae-518dfac40101" :question/math-academy-id "q-12040" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=5.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "207bcdce-2336-579a-87a6-8b38f5c5b78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253952} {:answer/id #uuid "3316ccea-5393-5fde-b5af-b1927ce7ccbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254112} {:answer/id #uuid "4d941473-4895-5924-9bfd-210373285ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254337} {:answer/id #uuid "51f02510-4584-5390-b37a-04704a64d7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254382} {:answer/id #uuid "717a5541-64cd-5b06-b0ea-5a6d9be6847c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254677} :answer-field/id #uuid "93384d39-abf4-5798-be0e-1efa952b50c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256191}] :question/id #uuid "179b0a83-f4d2-55fc-982f-7126c97476ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-12041" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057e6a8b-1fb2-59df-aeb5-575a9474cdaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=-x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275526} {:answer/id #uuid "40429c49-c4cf-52ed-9431-d37d2be295e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276037} {:answer/id #uuid "9720fc88-7765-5257-b97b-2fb81cb6a42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276834} {:answer/id #uuid "d1091080-ea45-50f2-a7bf-231ea9739d16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277326} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4cf5a9-6d28-5c29-a2e9-62b24e89e2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277326} :answer-field/id #uuid "90b36730-cb24-5752-8142-a1f0c9106ada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277981}] :question/id #uuid "b6efb939-92b8-5a77-8f54-81cda5e95098" :question/math-academy-id "q-159762" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/db/dbe3773dea369f6b58fc2ad45a32f98c2c9ae356701baf3ab56af3daa6ca732d.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection across the $x$-axis."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "571bd14d-e76e-51d3-8cbb-b23e385e1794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346093} {:answer/id #uuid "74aa1911-f05c-57a6-a47e-050ef2ac8ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346381} {:answer/id #uuid "b0011ab7-234f-5ab2-8039-dd7a76e9e304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346885} {:answer/id #uuid "b3332789-f827-55b9-8dc7-d8aa5b63e387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346915} {:answer/id #uuid "d619cc6b-8419-5273-9a8c-a0a4ef568d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346885} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f7dfee-86fe-517f-a5a2-aba244eb24db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347717}] :question/id #uuid "696c9d74-4ea0-5608-ba1a-980f930f11c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-78301" :question/problem "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=x?$" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is $T=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/0e/0e37a258ea833a2d490fc34a34af40a5c7a18f7589f107c6d0ed631b331c8f2a.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4330aa67-8eca-534c-a9e9-91a37ada11b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345930} {:answer/id #uuid "551607ae-79d2-5c83-af3d-a8635eff305f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{17}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346072} {:answer/id #uuid "65d47725-4eb6-598c-b932-230b8b362a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346239} {:answer/id #uuid "78f8d6ef-022c-5f56-9e15-fc6e37365741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346409} {:answer/id #uuid "cacbfb3c-c88b-5545-93e1-cb25164a4ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347121} :answer-field/id #uuid "526ad53a-59d3-5db8-9e7d-1c337e0505d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347747}] :question/id #uuid "4db462f3-5435-5b8e-8538-abab7a997273" :question/math-academy-id "q-78337" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=17.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $17.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db71c30-5b1d-5950-a3dc-c15f25376984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348847} {:answer/id #uuid "303ab460-0ec3-5c48-913e-ac1811f6a395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348875} {:answer/id #uuid "465b8c7c-6d48-5c20-a251-1b2c4f230